fr:mainmatter.html:p:
Krull's height theorem gives \operatorname {ht} J \le  \frac {n(n+1)}{2}
unconditionally, that is \dim  V(J) \ge  \frac {n(n - 1)}{2}, and
the flag witnesses attain that lower bound.

